From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:24:31 +0200
Subject: usb: musb: sunxi: Enable internal DMA on the H3/H5

The H3 and H5 have the same USB-OTG internal DMA engine as the A64.
Declare it on the sun8i-h3 compatible (shared by both SoCs). DTs that
don't describe the "dma" register region - including H616 boards that
match through the h3 fallback - keep working through the existing PIO
fallback in probe, at the cost of a probe-time warning.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/usb/musb/Kconfig | 3 ++-
 drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c | 8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/Kconfig b/drivers/usb/musb/Kconfig
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/Kconfig
@@ -159,7 +159,8 @@ config USB_SUNXI_IDMA
 	  It is not Mentor's engine, but it is driven through the same
 	  software mode-select CSR paths.
 
-	  Only the A64 is supported; other sunxi SoCs fall back to PIO.
+	  The A83T, H3/H5 and A64 are supported; other sunxi SoCs fall
+	  back to PIO.
 
 config USB_TI_CPPI41_DMA
 	bool 'TI CPPI 4.1'
diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c b/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/sunxi.c
@@ -348,9 +348,10 @@ static void sunxi_musb_disable(struct musb *musb)
  * etc.) around channel_program(); we only drive the idma engine and
  * report completion via musb_dma_completion().
  *
- * Only the A64 has this engine; sunxi_musb_dma_controller_create()
- * refuses to build a controller unless the matched SoC declares it, so
- * every other sunxi SoC stays on PIO with a NULL dma_controller.
+ * The A83T, H3/H5 and A64 have this engine;
+ * sunxi_musb_dma_controller_create() refuses to build a controller
+ * unless the matched SoC declares it, so every other sunxi SoC stays on
+ * PIO with a NULL dma_controller.
  * ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
 
 /* Offsets into the "dma" register region, not the core's. */
@@ -1385,6 +1386,7 @@ static const struct sunxi_musb_cfg sun8i_h3_musb_cfg = {
 	.hdrc_config = &sunxi_musb_hdrc_config_4eps,
 	.has_reset = true,
 	.no_configdata = true,
+	.has_idma = true,
 };
 
 static const struct sunxi_musb_cfg sun50i_a64_musb_cfg = {
-- 
Armbian

